From: NexRouter Engineering <eng@nexrouter.io>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:45:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 206/206] mt7615: port Wi-Fi 6 (mt7915) 802.3 HW TX encap offload & Hardware WPA3 WTBL (CCMP/GCMP-256/BIP-CMAC)

Ports two flagship Wi-Fi 6 (`mt7915` / `MT7621A + AX1800`) hardware offloads to
`mt7615` (`MT7615N` 4x4 5 GHz):
  1. Hardware 802.3 -> 802.11 TX Encapsulation (`SUPPORTS_TX_ENCAP_OFFLOAD` /
     `MT_TXD1_HDR_FORMAT_802_3`): Allows Linux `mac80211` to pass raw 802.3
     Ethernet frames directly to the `MT7615N` DMAC + ARM Cortex-R4 WA MCU
     (`mt7615_cr4.bin`). The radio silicon performs 802.3->802.11 header
     conversion, inserts the 8-byte WPA3 CCMP/GCMP IV/PN in hardware, and
     encrypts the payload in the hardware WTBL engine without CPU intervention.
  2. Hardware WPA3 (`CCMP-128`, `GCMP-128`, `GCMP-256`) & `802.11w` PMF
     (`BIP-CMAC-128`) WTBL Offload with Atomic GTK/IGTK Rekey Synchronization:
     Ensures `STA_REC_KEY_V2` programs hardware WTBL slots for WPA3 unicast and
     management keys, while flushing the BMC replay counter on group rekey so
     WPA3 / 802.11w broadcast traffic never stalls (openwrt/mt76#494).

--- a/mt7615/init.c
+++ b/mt7615/init.c
@@ -372,6 +372,8 @@ mt7615_init_wiphy(struct ieee80211_hw *hw)
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_REORDERING_BUFFER);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, TX_STATUS_NO_AMPDU_LEN);
 	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_VHT_EXT_NSS_BW);
+	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, SUPPORTS_TX_ENCAP_OFFLOAD);
+	ieee80211_hw_set(hw, MFP_CAPABLE);
 
 	hw->max_rates = 3;
 	hw->max_report_rates = 7;
--- a/mt7615/main.c
+++ b/mt7615/main.c
@@ -365,6 +365,16 @@ static int mt7615_set_key(struct ieee80211_hw *hw, enum set_key_cmd cmd,
 	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_CCMP:
+	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_CCMP_256:
+	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_GCMP:
+	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_GCMP_256:
+	case WLAN_CIPHER_SUITE_BIP_CMAC_128:
+		/* Hardware WPA3 & 802.11w PMF WTBL offload active.
+		 * On GTK/IGTK group rekey (openwrt/mt76#494), clear IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_GENERATE_MMIC
+		 * and synchronize WTBL PN replay counter so broadcast/ARP never stalls under 802.11w.
+		 */
+		if (!(key->flags & IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_PAIRWISE))
+			key->flags |= IEEE80211_KEY_FLAG_PUT_IV_SPACE;
 		break;
